# --- Tufelli_masonry_typeC ---
# Patched/reworked masonry, mixed exposed stone and infill/repairs, brick dentil cornice, evidence of blocked former openings
# Evidence: A-417/417_a (WhatsApp Image 2023-06-01 at 14.50.44/45/46, 14.51.48/49/50): exposed stone interspersed with rendered patches and a decorative brick course
# Flag: Scores kept uniformly low across all 7 parameters per the manuscript's explicit statement that this residential fabric has 'more frequent use of reused bricks, and greater variability in coursing and joint execution' than the representative architecture its local-technique description is based on - a stated characterisation from the manuscript, not read off any single photo
:Tufelli_masonry_typeC a hmo:MasonryWall ;
    rdfs:label "Tufelli_masonry_typeC" ;
    hsv:hasDocument :SurveyCampaign_20230601, :CaseStudyManuscript ;
